# Build context for backend/Dockerfile, whose build context is the repo root.
#
# Today both COPY instructions are scoped to backend/, so most of this file changes nothing about
# what lands in the image. It is written for the day someone widens a COPY to `. /app` — at that
# moment the difference between "1.4 MB of Python" and "a published image containing .env.production
# and a Firebase service-account key" is only this file. Deny-list the dangerous things now, while
# it costs nothing, rather than after the credential is in a layer on a registry.
#
# Rules are deny-list, not allow-list, on purpose: a `*` catch-all plus re-includes silently drops
# newly added backend directories, and the failure mode is a container that boots and 500s.

# --- Secrets. The reason this file exists. ------------------------------------
# The bare name and every flavour (.env.production, .env.local, .env.staging), matching .gitignore.
.env
.env.*
# ...except the example, which holds only placeholders and is useful documentation inside an image.
!.env.example
# Firebase admin credentials. Named file plus the pattern the console hands out by default, because
# the second one arrives with a different filename every time it is regenerated.
firebase-service-account.json
*firebase-adminsdk*.json
*service-account*.json
# Anything that is obviously key material, wherever it sits in the tree.
*.pem
*.key
*.p12
*.pfx
id_rsa*
.npmrc
.netrc

# --- Version control and tooling metadata ------------------------------------
.git
.gitignore
.github
.dockerignore
.claude
.md
docs
README.md

# --- Dependencies. Reinstalled inside the image from requirements.txt. ---------
node_modules
**/node_modules
.venv
venv
__pycache__
**/__pycache__
*.py[cod]
.pytest_cache
.mypy_cache
.ruff_cache

# --- Build output. Rebuilt in the image, or belongs to the frontend, which does not ship here. ---
apps/web/dist
apps/*/dist
dist
build
coverage
.expo
# collectstatic output: the Dockerfile runs collectstatic itself, so a stale host copy would be
# copied in and then overwritten. Keeping it out also keeps the context small.
backend/staticfiles
staticfiles

# --- Local state that must never become part of an image ----------------------
backend/db.sqlite3
*.sqlite3
*.sqlite
*.db
# celery beat's schedule database, written into ./backend by the bind mount in compose.yaml.
backend/celerybeat-schedule
backend/celerybeat-schedule.*
celerybeat.pid
*.log
media/
backend/media/

# --- Test fixtures. Derived by backend/datamock/make_fixtures.py, which is kept. ---------------
backend/datamock/*
!backend/datamock/make_fixtures.py
!backend/datamock/README.md

# --- Frontend source. Not used by backend/Dockerfile, and megabytes of it. ------
# apps/web/public alone is ~104 MB of imagery and MediaPipe binaries; leaving it in the context
# means uploading it to the daemon on every build for nothing.
apps
packages
package.json
package-lock.json
uv.lock
.python-version

# --- Editor / OS noise --------------------------------------------------------
.DS_Store
**/.DS_Store
.idea
.vscode
*.swp
Thumbs.db
